((date 2026-11-25) (slug universe-depth)
 (hypothesis
  "USER 2026-11-23, after the NAV-scale read (#3704): try expanding the universe, with no structural floor. At a 100k account the universe (top-3000) and the No_structural_stop gate are what keep cheap names out; this run tests both. Pre-registered in dev/experiments/universe-depth-2026-11-23/PREREG.md (237b2bb8d228, #3707) and PREREG-ADDENDUM.md (376b2f5ab059, #3719, written blind before results). Arms on the record spec rk-k0..k4 at live size (initial_cash 100k + dev/weekly-picks/live-size-overrides.sexp): S3 = pit-v13 top-3000 (control), U4 = pit-v13 top-4000, N3 = top-3000 + require_structural_stop false, UN4 = top-4000 + require_structural_stop false. Reads: U4 vs S3 (depth), N3 vs S3 (structural stop), UN4 vs U4 (secondary). Rule: paired delta ln(arm/control) per seed; PASS median >= +0.20, >= 4/5 positive, median dDD <= +3 pp; HARM median <= -0.20, >= 4/5 negative; a V6-failing seed is dropped, < 4 valid seeds = INVALID.")
 (base_scenario
  "universe-depth-2026-11-23: 20 cells (S3/U4/N3/UN4 x k0-k4), kit ca42b9146 (#3714), build SC_SHA ca42b914644506b1a305f158fed4340f36387772, image sha256:886851cbc0f1, warehouse v13pit-12710 + corpact-2026-11-23 + bars data-20261123, record spec rk-kK 2000-01-01 -> 2026-06-26 at initial_cash 100k with the live-size liquidity overrides, five Claude cloud routines launched 2026-11-24; TRIPWIRE MATCH 5/5 (ns-P-100k-k0 trades.csv md5 f7746eb838618c9eac4aed7f969e63af, 563 lines); V6 DIFFER on 15/15 pairs; mark-free artifacts in results/k0..k4 (PR #3721), price-bearing files in the private results repo")
